    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate's opening gross claims outstanding at 1 January 2019 was GBP 902.565m. Analysis of the gross claims development triangle indicates a net favourable prior-year reserve movement of approximately GBP 41.7m (a release of reserves), driven by releases across a number of older underwriting years that outweighed adverse development on specific prior catastrophe events. The Annual Report nonetheless highlights adverse development on certain prior catastrophe events (notably Typhoon Jebi and the California Camp wildfire) and a run-off deficit on prior accident years on a net basis in the technical account narrative, with the reinsurance acceptances portfolio showing a deficit while direct business showed a small surplus.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "2019 was not impacted by any new catastrophe events, but rather various large risk losses, particularly in the Marine sector, in addition to deterioration on prior year catastrophe events (Typhoon Jebi and Camp Wildfire).",
      "The profit on the technical account of GBP 31.2m (2018: profit GBP 38.9m) includes a run-off deficit of GBP 18.5m for prior accident years (2018: GBP 44.0m surplus).",
      "This included a deficit of GBP 22.8m for reinsurance acceptance business and a surplus of GBP 4.3m on direct business.",
      "2019 also suffered from a number of large losses, Star Centurion (gross loss GBP 6.8m, net GBP 5.9m), Deer Park (gross loss GBP 6.4m, net GBP 4m), Jim Beam (gross loss GBP 8.9m, net GBP 3.9m) and Badr (gross loss GBP 5.3m, net GBP 4.0m).",
      "Additionally, personal lines incurred losses GBP 12.0m."
